# vergeio_user (Resource)
Create a user

## Example Usage

This example queries the group data source to get the Key (ID) of the Administrators group, creates a user, and assigns the user as a member of Administrators. `vergeio_user` manages a VergeOS user account.

{{ tffile "examples/resources/vergeio_user/resource.tf" }}

`password` is stored in state. It is deprecated and will be removed in v4. `password_wo` is sent on create and again when `password_wo_version` changes. Terraform stores the version, not the password. Changing `password_wo` without changing the version does not update the user. `password_wo` requires Terraform 1.11 or OpenTofu 1.11. Do not set both.

{{ tffile "examples/resources/vergeio_user/resource_writeonly.tf" }}
<!-- schema generated by tfplugindocs -->
## Arguments

### Required

- `name` (String)

### Optional

- `auth_source` (Number) - Key (ID) of the auth source to attach the user to. If left blank the user will be created as a local user.
- `change_password` (Boolean) - Default = False
- `displayname` (String)
- `email` (String)
- `enabled` (Boolean) - Default = True
- `password` (String, Sensitive) - Deprecated. Stored in state through v3.x. Use `password_wo`. It will be removed in v4.
- `password_wo` (String, Sensitive, Write-Only) - Sent on create and when `password_wo_version` changes. Not stored. Requires Terraform 1.11 or OpenTofu 1.11. Do not set `password` as well.
- `password_wo_version` (Number) - Increment to change `password_wo`. Terraform stores this number, not the password.
- `remote_name` (String) - Depends on `auth_source`. Only necessary when the remote username differs from the username (name).
- `type` (String) - The type of user being created. Normal is the default without specification.
    - `normal`
    - `api`
    - `vdi`

### Read-Only

- `id` (String) - ID of this resource.